{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment2.md","content":"⚠️ **IMPORTANT: kicker + merge-trigger are flipped but guarded by nothing — the promised "every awf uses" invariant is not enforced**

The PR description's mitigation says the guard asserts *"every awf uses: is exactly main (never a stale SHA, never a random ref)"*, but the guard's `stubs` map covers only three legs:

```dart
// test/machine_kit/factory_stub_ref_test.dart
final stubs = <String, (String, String)>{
  'ai-teammate.yml': (teammate, 'factory-teammate.yml'),
  'machine-sm.yml':  (sm, 'factory-sm.yml'),
  'machine-merge.yml': (merge, 'factory-merge.yml'),
};
```

`sm-kicker.yml` and `merge-trigger.yml` — two of the five files this PR edits — are invisible to it. The unlisted-stub-escapes-all-checks hazard is documented in the map's own doc comment ("New stubs MUST be added here"); this PR adds two new caller classes without adding them. Under the new policy the regression to catch is exactly "one leg re-pinned to a stale SHA or a random ref while the rest track main" — extend the map to all five so that stays mechanically enforced.

Related inconsistency the extended map must settle: `merge-trigger.yml` delegates with `secrets: inherit` (pre-existing), while the guard enforces explicit `SOURCE_GITHUB_TOKEN` mapping on the other three stubs.
"}

